# Copy to .env and fill in. NAMES ONLY HERE -- never a value.
# .env is git-ignored; this file is not.

# --- required by the package -------------------------------------------------
# Both are read at connect time when `client_id` / `access_token` are left None
# on the client configs, which is the recommended way: a Nautilus config is
# serialisable, and a token in one is a token in whatever wrote it out.
#
# THE ACCESS TOKEN LIVES 24 HOURS from the moment it is minted -- `exp` is
# exactly `iat + 86400`, measured. Not from a fixed hour, so a token minted
# during market hours dies during market hours.
DHAN_CLIENT_ID=
DHAN_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- the second switch on live orders ----------------------------------------
# LEAVE THIS UNSET unless you intend to place real orders with real money.
#
# Submission requires this AND `live_orders=True` on DhanExecClientConfig. Two
# switches rather than one, because a stray import cannot set an environment
# variable and a stray environment variable cannot construct a client. The
# value is compared exactly: `true`, `yes` and `0` all do nothing.
#
# NAUTILUS_INDIA_LIVE_ORDERS=1

# --- not read by the package -------------------------------------------------
# Convention only, for manual probing against https://sandbox.dhan.co. The
# sandbox needs no IP whitelisting, which makes it the only way to exercise the
# write path from an ordinary machine -- but it is not production, and it has
# no matching engine, so nothing placed there ever fills.
# DHAN_SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID=
# DHAN_SANDBOX_TOKEN=
